        "raw": "<p>Now that I've got a print-and-play in hand (thanks for making isolation a little more fun, &gt;G!) I've noticed a couple things that I want to make sure I interpreted correctly before trying this new spirit in game.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n1. Share Secrets of Survival: \"Each time Dahan would be Destroyed ..., Destroy 2 fewer Dahan.\" Because of the proper use of \"Destroy,\" I assume this only refers to destruction via the word \"Destroy\" on spirit cards, events, etc., and not to destruction via taking damage that reduces the Dahan's health to zero. Correct?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. Study the Invaders' Fears: \"Turn the top card of the Fear Deck face-up.\" I assume I should interpret this text as literally as possible without interfering with existing Fear card rules, so...</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>The now-face-up card stays on top of the Fear Deck (it's not earned, we just get to read what it says).</li>\r\n\t<li>When the face-up card is earned via accumulating Fear Tokens, it moves to the earned Fear area and stays face-up.</li>\r\n\t<li>Additional use of this power essentially has no effect (it turns a card face-up that was already face up) until the top face-up card is earned, and reveals a face-down card on the top of the Fear Deck.</li>\r\n\t<li>If I use this power and then the players earn 2 fear cards before the next Invader Phase, we place the 2nd card face-down on top of the face-up card in the earned fear card area. (Is it kosher to uncover the face-up card to read its effects?) When we are supposed to flip the cards and resolve their effects, we would turn both cards face-up, first resolve the card that Shifting Memory revealed and we earned first, and then the next earned card.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Thanks! I'm looking forward to the new spirit!</p>",
